<title>UK: MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS BRITISH GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS BRITISH GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>SILVERSTONE, England 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacques  Villeneuve of Canada, driving a Williams, won the British Grand Prix motor race on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Jean Alesi of France finished second in a Benetton, with Alexander Wurz of Austria, also in a Benetton third.</p>
<p>Britain's David Coulthard finished fourth in a McLaren, with Germany's Ralf Schumacher fifth in a Jordan and Britain's Damon Hill sixth in an Arrows.  </p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after nine rounds):</p>
<p>  1. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    47</p>
<p>  2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     43</p>
<p>  3. Jean Alesi (France)			 21</p>
<p>  4. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany)	 19</p>
<p>  5. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    18</p>
<p>  6. Olivier Panis (France)		    15</p>
<p>  7. David Coulthard (Britain)		 14</p>
<p>  8 equal. Gerhard Berger  (Germany)	 10</p>
<p>  8 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p> 10. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)	     8</p>
<p> 11 equal. Johnny Herbert (Britain)	   7</p>
<p> 11 equal. Ralf Schumacher (Germany)	  7</p>
<p> 13. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 14. Alexander Wurz (Austria		    4</p>
<p> 15. Mika Salo (Finland)			  2</p>
<p> 16 equal. Nicola Larini (Italy)		1</p>
<p> 16 equal. Shinji Nakano (Japan)		1</p>
<p> 16 equal. Damon Hill (Britain)		 1</p>
